Day 50 – Kubernetes Architecture and Cluster Setup

✅ Learned Kubernetes architecture and why it is used.

What I did

- Installed "kubectl"
- Set up a local Kubernetes cluster
- Explored Kubernetes Control Plane and Worker Node components
- Verified the cluster using "kubectl get nodes"
- Explored "kube-system" pods
- Learned the role of API Server, etcd, Scheduler, Controller Manager, kubelet, kube-proxy, and Container Runtime

Key Learning

Today I started my Kubernetes journey and understood how Kubernetes manages containerized applications at scale. I also learned how the control plane and worker nodes work together to keep applications running reliably.

